                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>Distribution of childcare among mothers, fathers and non-parental providers in households with pre-school children. Composition of household / employment of parents before and after birth of child, children / type of childcare for preschool children in household and whether childcare was necessary due to work or other activities of parents / type of childcare for children older than 4 years in household / making use of parental leave / whether respondent can choose between different types of childcare / prices of childcare facilities / quality and satisfaction concerning childcare / time spent at domestic tasks and care for children / values and beliefs of respondents concerning division of labour and care for children between women and men, and upbringing of children / income and education / advise of respondent concerning childcare policy of the government. Background variables: basic characteristics/ household characteristics/ place of work/ occupation/employment/ income/capital assets/ education</p>"
